<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20409] Bind the NIDs to their local NUMA nodes by default</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20409</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Right now, if the LNet is not configured, a NID won't be bound to its own NUMA node, which will lead to suboptimal throughput during testing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Asking every customer to configure LNet on the client is a big usability issue, LNet should be able to bind the NIDs to their own NUMA node by default, probably it should even override the config.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This setting is so obvious to me that I'm not sure if I'm missing some contexts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=adilger" class="user-hover" rel="adilger"&gt;adilger&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=hornc" class="user-hover" rel="hornc"&gt;hornc&lt;/a&gt; please feel free to comment.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
